      "text": [
        " : قُلْتُ لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ رَأَيْتُ فِي ثَوْبِي شَيْئاً مِنْ دَمٍ وَ أَنَا أَطُوفُ قَالَ «فَاعْرِفِ اَلْمَوْضِعَ ثُمَّ اُخْرُجْ فَاغْسِلْهُ ثُمَّ عُدْ فَابْنِ عَلَى طَوَافِكَ »."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2793 - Yunus ibn Ya‘qub narrated: I said to Abu Abdullah (as), \"I noticed some blood on my clothing while I was performing tawaf.\"\nImam (as) said: \"Mark the spot where you stopped, then exit, wash it off, and return to continue your tawaf from where you left off.\""
        ]
      }
